* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- floor and roof slabs
* Composite slab: 3 in metal deck with 4.5 in of concrete above the ribs; the SHELL has the average
* concrete thickness, 6 in = 0.5 ft.  The shell nodes are the beam nodes (no offset), so the slab is
* not composite with the beams here: the vertical frequencies of the floors are lower bounds.  The
* slab is the floor diaphragm: no rigid-diaphragm constraint is needed.
* Group 9: floors 1 and 2, 6 x 4 shells of 10 ft x 10 ft per floor (1-24 floor 1, 25-48 floor 2)
