* Column bases.  The eight moment-frame columns (line B, and A2, A3, C2, C3 of lines 2 and 3) are
* fixed: base plates and anchor rods designed for the moment.  A single mat node can take the column
* moment without a rigid spider (example 1 needs one for its shear-wall stick): the rotational
* stiffness of the 4 ft mat at a node, 1.3E7 kip ft/rad (the HOUSE stiffness of the mat condensed to its
* rotations, translations held), is about 170 times the 4 E I / L of a W14x132 column (7.7E4 kip ft/rad).
* The four corner columns are braced-frame and gravity columns: pinned (KI releases M2 and M3 at the
* base node I; the torsion M1 stays).
KI,1,4,3,0,0,0,0,1,1
KI,9,12,3,0,0,0,0,1,1
